 "note": "Simulation of the design trap (plan D14 item 2): accidents that generate their own event reports pull the\nwithin-plant-year estimate below the truth, and removing reports from the accident day and the 2 days after brings\nit back.\n\nReal event counts and the primary panel's plant-years and accident counts; no real accident dates. Each draw places\neach plant-year's accidents on random at-risk days of that plant-year:\n  (a) no effect: uniformly;\n  (b) planted 1.3 per doubling: with probability proportional to (1 + events in the 90-day window) ** log2(1.3).\nEach simulated accident adds reports at its plant at the observed excess, computed from\ndata/manifests/stored_checks.json: Poisson((212 - 9.7) / 541 = 0.374) on the accident day and Poisson(0.006) on each\nof the 2 days after (26 reports on those days against 19.4 expected). (A first run used 0.03 for the 2 days after,\nwhich overstated the excess; plan D16 item 2.) Fits: naive (90 and 365-day windows) and\nwith the reports of the accident day and the 2 days after removed. 20 draws per scenario.",
